# MCP tool names and what the pre-tool hook decides for each, one
# "<deny|ask|allow> <tool name> [<tool input as JSON>]" per line, the input
# {} when left out. Every case runs in the main session, as commands.cases
# does. The names cover every form seen on this machine and the trackers the
# plan names. "allow" means the hook stays out, and Claude Code's own
# permission settings decide.
#
# Posting: comment, reply, review, reaction, send_message, post_message,
# schedule_message.
deny mcp__github__add_issue_comment
deny mcp__github__create_pull_request_review
deny mcp__github__add_pull_request_review_comment_to_pending_review
deny mcp__github__reply_to_review_comment
deny mcp__slack__slack_send_message
deny mcp__slack__slack_post_message
deny mcp__slack__slack_schedule_message
deny mcp__slack__slack_add_reaction
deny mcp__linear__create_comment
deny mcp__5c236953-16e0-40fd-98e4-3923bdf825ae__notion-create-comment
deny mcp__c64407bc-b8f7-494b-bb48-1cb85ff2b0d5__comment-on-design
deny mcp__c64407bc-b8f7-494b-bb48-1cb85ff2b0d5__reply-to-comment
deny mcp__jira__addCommentToJiraIssue
deny mcp__fibery__postComment
